Subject: Running INLA on multiple nodes
Message-ID: <aMcWJSBNb88.W04gK_i2AwAJ@r-inla-discussion-group.groups.google.com>
Archived-At: <https://groups.google.com/g/r-inla-discussion-group/c/aMcWJSBNb88/m/W04gK_i2AwAJ>
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset="utf-8"
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Dear INLA-community,

I'm currently runinng a negative binomial / zero inflated poisson (not decided yet) model with a Besags ICAR model on a single node with 20 cores and 6,4GB RAM each (total 128GB). At the moment I'm only performing tests with a sub-sample of my dataset. Running on 1000 observations took 3 mins, 5000 observations took >1h (hit the wall). Negative binomial seems to use all cores by default, whereas zip0 only uses 16. However I have about 45000 observations and more data might come in. Therefore, I'm a bit afraid that the model might run for several days (3 days is the upper wall limit).  Is there any possible of running INLA on multiple nodes to speed up the process? Or can you suggest any modifications that might help?

Any hints will be highly appreciated!

Best,
Alexander

