Hi,

Sorry to be a pain, but that still doesn’t fully describe the size and structure of your model. When you increase the number of observations, is your spatial domain increasing as well, or are the observations filling up a fixed region? In the latter case, your adjacency structure will get relatively denser and denser, which will be more expensive. Also, for such neighborhoods the basic car model where all neighbours are weighted equally can lead to non-intuitive joint model behaviour. For example, when applied to a second order neighborhood structure on a lattice, it can results in negative correlations!

Finn

